sk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Newsmax, Inc. is a small-cap communication services business with a $1.2B market cap on $189M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -117% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 39%.","The company is burning through $107M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -4310.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.1%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 22% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (63.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Communication Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 61% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 711% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":7.113170428660178},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $6.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cord-cutting acceleration and audience fragmentation \u2014 legacy distribution bundles unravel faster than subscription revenue can replace them.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Upgrades for November 13th (ADSK, DAVE, DPZ, DTM, ECL, ENGN, LFTO, NMAX, NMG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/investment-analysts-upgrades-for-november-13th-adsk-dave-dpz-dtm-ecl-engn-lfto-nmax-nmg.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794595487.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Newsmax (NMAX) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/newsmax-nmax-q3-2026-earnings-052015000.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794547397.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Newsmax Inc (NMAX) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Revenue, Second Straight Positive ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/media-advertising/articles/newsmax-inc-nmax-q3-2026-050250055.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546170.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why Newsmax Stock Popped on Friday","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-newsmax-stock-popped-friday-232202952.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794612122.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Newsmax Reports Record Quarterly Revenues, Big Jump in Net Income","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/media-advertising/articles/newsmax-reports-record-quarterly-revenues-192704837.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794598024.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"ti